Kontrol-ID manages Kontrol's standalone multithread secure web gateway for
transparent Windows user identification or explicit proxy authentication. It
provides native Kerberos/SPNEGO, opt-in NTLMv2/Winbind, and HTTP Basic
authentication through the Kontrol local or LDAP server, assisted AD/keytab
enrollment, policy-group mapping, TLS inspection, a fallback login portal and
XMLRPC configuration synchronization.

No Squid process or persistent Kontrol service on Windows endpoints is required.
Kerberos is the recommended explicit authentication method; NTLMv2 is retained
for legacy domain clients and Basic is limited to trusted client networks.
